**Q7**. Using the answer from A5 as a starting point, produce a summary table that has the following information for each recipient: \* count of contributions \* total amount of all contributions \* the average contribution amount \* the median contribution amount \* the smallest contribution amount \* the largest contribution amount

Store it as a variable object called `wv_summary` so that you can examine it with the data viewer. What newsworthy nuggets jump out at you that you could imagine dropping into a news story? Write a few summary sentences with overall findings.

**A7**.
More than four times as many people donated to the Trump National Committee as to the next-most popular recipient--which was the Trump Save America PAC. It would be interesting to compare that ratio to the amount of Democratic donations to presidential candidates on ActBlue, to see if the Republican base is specifically obsessed with Trump or if this is just what always happens during presidential election years. Also, Eli Crane for Congress is weirdly high up on the list for someone who was not a sitting member of Congress at the time. He's in 17th place, which is ahead of major Senate candidates like Marco Rubio, Kari Lake and Dave McCormick, and he's noticeably ahead of most other swing-seat House candidates.
```{r}
wv_summary<- wv_winred_contributions |>
  group_by(memo_text) |>
  summarise(
    count_contribs = n(),
    total_amount = sum(amount),
    mean_amount = mean(amount),
    median_amount = median(amount),
